    "id": "b8886e91dc52e8a5456b831a",
    "path": "datafusion_ffi::proto::logical_extension_codec::FFI_LogicalExtensionCodec::new",
    "name": "new",
    "owner": "datafusion_ffi::proto::logical_extension_codec::FFI_LogicalExtensionCodec",
    "crate": "datafusion-ffi",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn new(codec: Arc<dyn LogicalExtensionCodec>, runtime: Option<Handle>, task_ctx_provider: impl Into<FFI_TaskContextProvider>) -> Self",
    "docs": "Creates a new [`FFI_LogicalExtensionCodec`].\n\nIf `codec` is already foreign, this re-exports its original FFI handle\nrather than adding another wrapper layer. The handle still adopts the\n`task_ctx_provider` supplied here, so it is never silently discarded and\nan imported codec can be rebound to a different session.\n\n`runtime` is only honored when a new wrapper is created. An\nalready-foreign handle keeps the runtime of the library that owns it,\nbecause that value lives in private data this side cannot reach.",
